# Motion PPT Cursor Rules
# Always adhere to AGENTS.md and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md.

## Core Philosophy: Editable-First
1. Prioritize PowerPoint native & composite animations over rasterized/rendered video.
2. Text, cards, and shapes must remain 100% editable in PowerPoint unless explicitly instructed as a 3D/shader effect.

## Monorepo Dependency Rules
- @motion-ppt/shared: Zero internal dependencies.
- @motion-ppt/core: Pure domain model & scene graph. NEVER import Three.js, React, or MCP here.
- @motion-ppt/animation: Timeline, Easing, Effect Registry, and Animation DSL.
- @motion-ppt/pptx: PptxGenJS + OOXML Timing Patch Engine.
- apps/mcp-server: MCP Tools exposing domain operations to AI agents.

## Code Standards
- Strict TypeScript: No 'any'. Use 'unknown' with narrowing.
- All new effects must implement EffectDefinition and register in EffectRegistry.
- Animation plans must adhere to docs/ANIMATION-DSL-SPEC.md.
- Consult skills/ directory before writing animation logic.
